# Intent–Delivery naming for requirements & plans

**SSOT (cite, don't fork):**
[`ContextCore/docs/design/DETERMINISTIC_INTENT_DELIVERY_LANGUAGE_OVERVIEW.md`](../../../../ContextCore/docs/design/DETERMINISTIC_INTENT_DELIVERY_LANGUAGE_OVERVIEW.md)
and companion
[`DETERMINISTIC_INTENT_DELIVERY_LANGUAGE.md`](../../../../ContextCore/docs/design/DETERMINISTIC_INTENT_DELIVERY_LANGUAGE.md)
(prefer `~/Documents/dev/ContextCore/…`, not worktree forks).

## Going forward (mandatory)

1. **Do not lead new REQ/PLAN filenames with sequential integers** (`REQ-01-…`, `PLAN-03-…`, `REQ-08-…` as the *document* identity). Integer ordinals are not the product name of the work.
2. **Name design docs from the intent–delivery four-form contract** — one string cannot serve machines, humans, docs, and telemetry:
   | Form | Role | Example shape |
   |------|------|----------------|
   | Local key | Short *inside* one initiative (may keep `FR-*` / `FEAT-*` for parsers) | `FEAT-1`, `FR-10` |
   | Canonical ref | Stable machine identity | `cc:intent:<initiative>:feature:feat-1` |
   | Semantic name | Human meaning (structured: action + object; actor/outcome as fields) | `Orient initiative work from the four-artifact dossier` |
   | Readable handle | Recognition + compact correlation | `feature/orient-initiative-work-from-…-<12hex>` |
3. **Prefer filenames/titles derived from semantic name or readable-handle slug**, scoped by kind, e.g.:
   - `REQ-sdk-node-home.md` / `PLAN-sdk-node-home.md`, or
   - `requirement/sdk-node-as-node-home-<suffix>.md`
   — not `REQ-01-sdk-node-home.md` solely because it was “the first phase.”
4. **Keep det-req in-body `FR-*` local keys** when writing det-req/0.1 — the language explicitly does **not** rename those (parser continuity). The ban is on **integer-led design-doc / phase branding**, not on FR bullets inside a requirement file.
5. **Distinguish product capability (`CAP-*` intent) from code capability** (capability-index / A2A). Same English word, different objects.
6. When linking phases of a ladder (e.g. viz Phase 3 authoring seat), identify the *initiative / feature / semantic outcome*, not “Phase N” or “REQ-0N” as the durable name.

## When creating or renaming docs

- Draft semantic name first (action + observable object); avoid bare attractors: support / manage / improve / enhance / handle / enable (advisory).
- Put initiative id + kind in the header or front-matter when a canonical ref exists or is planned.
- Update cross-links; do not leave integer-led aliases as the only title in new work.

## Legacy

Existing `REQ-01-*` / `PLAN-01-*` / `REQ-06-*` files may remain until deliberately renamed. **New** authoring follows this rule. Do not mint another integer-led pair for Phase 3 — use intent-language naming from the start.
